Let the instance's own OIDC provider create accounts while public signup is off.

On Cloudron the OIDC provider is the server's user directory and its access
control decides who may use the app, so SIGNUP_ENABLED=false (no public
password registration) plus OIDC_SIGNUP_ENABLED=true lets every permitted
Cloudron user sign in without an invitation.

